invariant: INV-17
file: poly1305_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh poly1305-avx2
reason: poly1305_avx2_blocks ends with VZEROUPPER where it had VZEROALL,
  as it already clears the upper halves before carry_scalar (decision
  110). The low halves still hold powers of r and the lanes' sums when
  the function returns, and under gcc 13.3 words of the accumulator that
  carry_scalar packed in xmm0 to xmm3. r and a tag seen on the wire give
  the pad. No wipe written in C names a register, and every tag is right.
  bin/poly1305_equiv_test sets every bit of ymm0 to ymm15, calls the
  kernel and stores the sixteen registers in one block of assembly, and
  requires every stored word zero. The kernel has a body on x86-64 alone,
  so the catch is the script, which builds the binary for x86-64 and runs
  it under qemu-x86_64, whose max model has AVX2 on every host. The lane
  skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    _mm256_zeroall();
--- new
    _mm256_zeroupper();
